#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# dawson_f

#% text
# `dawson_f(x)` gives Dawson's integral e^(-x^2) times the integral of e^(t^2) from 0 to x.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Numerical values as sqrt(pi)/2 e^(-x^2) erfi(x); `dawson_f` is odd.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
dawson_f(1.0)
#% output
#= 0.5380795069127684

#% cell
dawson_f(0)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
dawson_f(-x)
#% output
#= -dawson_f(x)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `erfi`, `erf`
